\f0\cf1\fs48\b SCOTTWARE\b0\par
\cf2\fs36\b PaintMac\b0\par
\fs24 A Scottware utility\par
Create. Edit. Make it yours.\par
\par
\fs28\b Install in three steps\b0\fs24\par
\par
1. Drag Scottware PaintMac.app onto the Applications shortcut in this disk image.\par
\par
2. Eject the Scottware PaintMac disk image in Finder.\par
\par
3. Open Scottware PaintMac from your Applications folder.\par
\par
\b Requirements\b0\par
macOS 13 or newer. Use the Apple-Silicon installer for M-series Macs or the Intel installer for Intel Macs. The installer filename identifies the included architecture.\par
\par
\b Start creating\b0\par
Choose a tool on the left, pick a color, and draw. Add layers with the + button. Save a .paintmac project to preserve editable layers; export PNG or JPEG to share your work. See Help > Tools & Shortcuts for keyboard shortcuts.\par
\par
\b Updating\b0\par
Quit Scottware PaintMac before replacing an existing copy in Applications. Your saved project files are stored wherever you chose to save them.\par
\par
\b Build signing\b0\par
This build is ad-hoc signed for local use and is not notarized by Apple. macOS may require approval in System Settings > Privacy & Security when opening a downloaded copy.\par
\par
\b Uninstall\b0\par
Quit the app and move Scottware PaintMac from Applications to the Trash. Saved project files can be managed separately in Finder.\par
}
